🔹 Program 2: Area Calculator Using Function Overloading

📌 Description

This program demonstrates function overloading by calculating the area of different shapes using the same function name "calculateArea()".

The function is overloaded with different parameters:

- 🟦 Square — accepts one integer parameter ("side")
- ▭ Rectangle — accepts two integer parameters ("length", "width")
- 🔵 Circle — accepts one double parameter ("radius")

The compiler selects the appropriate "calculateArea()" function based on the number and data type of the arguments.

🎯 Concept Used

Compile-Time Polymorphism — Function Overloading

💡 Key Point

«The same function name can perform different operations when its parameter list is different.»
